IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-78, TARGETED: the Public Tenders Law, 5752-1992 ("the Law"), and the preference regulations made under it. Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two items, I1 then I2, as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the body that publishes a tender under the Law and the preference regulations. A row of references asks that body no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument and the dates it prints, a place in the regulations, a regulation as printed, a chapter heading, an instruction of the 2007 amending regulations, a section as printed, a law as printed,
-- an order as printed, a reference by number, a later instrument read, an item, and the questions asked of them.
-- No reference is stated here; they are in td78-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest instrument read.
-- Subsection letters are written with Latin names for the Hebrew letters the regulations use: (א) is Alef, (ב) is Bet, (ד) is Dalet; the chapters are `chapter Gimel` and `chapter Dalet`.
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the instruments'. A date typed as an issue date is the date the footer of the issue prints; it is NOT a commencement date.
-- A signature date and a date a section prints for the start of an instrument are typed separately, and only where a page prints one.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A way a fact was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page images, with the order's own page from an archive copy of the printed issue, not an official site`
    `page image of an archive copy of the printed issue, not an official site`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `not checked`

DECLARE `A kind of source` IS ONE OF
    `official: Sefer HaChukim from the Knesset's site`
    `aid: archive of the printed issue, not an official site`

DECLARE `A series of publication` IS ONE OF
    `Kovetz HaTakanot`
    `Sefer HaChukim`

DECLARE `A chapter` IS ONE OF
    `chapter Gimel`
    `chapter Dalet`

DECLARE `A subsection letter` IS ONE OF
    Alef
    Bet
    Dalet

-- An issue of Kovetz HaTakanot or Sefer HaChukim. The issue date is the one the footer prints.
-- The signature date and the date a section prints for the start of an instrument are NOTHING unless a deposited page prints one.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its series` IS A `A series of publication`
    `its issue number` IS A NUMBER
    `its issue date` IS A DATE
    `its signature date` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date a section of it prints for its start` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `where its file comes from` IS A `A kind of source`

-- A place in the preference regulations.
DECLARE `A place in the regulations` HAS
    `its regulation` IS A NUMBER
    `its subsection` IS A MAYBE `A subsection letter`

-- The heading of a chapter of the regulations, as an instrument printed it.
DECLARE `A chapter heading as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the chapter` IS A `A chapter`
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A regulation (or a subsection of one) as the 1995 print has it. `the provisions it names, as tokens` are the stretches of its words that are written as a number and a letter in brackets.
-- `the heading it is printed under` is the chapter heading above it on the same printed page, where the print shows one; NOTHING where none is typed.
DECLARE `A regulation as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its place` IS A `A place in the regulations`
    `its margin note` IS A STRING
    `its words` IS A STRING
    `the provisions it names, as tokens` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the heading it is printed under` IS A MAYBE `A chapter heading as printed`

DECLARE `A kind of instruction` IS ONE OF
    `deletion of words from the name`
    `repeal of a chapter`
    `repeal of a regulation`
    `deletion of words from a regulation`
    `application clause`

-- An item of the 2007 amending regulations, as printed.
-- `the words it deletes` are the words the item itself prints between its marks; `its words` are the whole of the item.
DECLARE `An item of an instrument` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its item number` IS A NUMBER
    `its margin note` IS A STRING
    `the kind` IS A `A kind of instruction`
    `the chapter it names` IS A MAYBE `A chapter`
    `the regulation it names` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the words it deletes` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A reference by number inside a regulation: the citing words print a token, the token names a place, and the print of that place is typed beside it.
DECLARE `A reference by number` HAS
    `the citing regulation` IS A `A regulation as printed`
    `the token the citing words print` IS A STRING
    `the place the token names` IS A `A place in the regulations`
    `the print of that place in 1995` IS A `A regulation as printed`

-- A paragraph an amending law prints inside quotation marks, with the number printed at its head and the margin note printed beside it.
DECLARE `A quoted paragraph` HAS
    `the number printed at its head` IS A NUMBER
    `the margin note printed beside it` IS A STRING
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A numbered section as an instrument printed it. `its words` are the words outside any quoted paragraph.
DECLARE `A section as printed` HAS
    `its number` IS A NUMBER
    `its margin note` IS A STRING
    `its words` IS A STRING
    `the quoted paragraph it prints` IS A MAYBE `A quoted paragraph`

-- A law as an instrument printed it: the title, the numbered sections, the footnotes.
DECLARE `A law as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its title` IS A STRING
    `its sections` IS A LIST OF `A section as printed`
    `its footnotes` IS A LIST OF STRING

-- An order as an instrument printed it. The opening words carry two pointers: a section number cited for the power, and a defined term for a law.
-- `the law the opening words define the term as` is the law value whose title is the title the opening words print before the term; the cross-references module tests that the two titles are the same string.
DECLARE `An order as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its title` IS A STRING
    `its opening words` IS A STRING
    `the section number the opening words cite for the power` IS A NUMBER
    `the title the opening words print before the defined term` IS A STRING
    `the law the opening words define the term as` IS A `A law as printed`
    `its sections` IS A LIST OF `A section as printed`
    `the section number its section 1 cites` IS A NUMBER
    `the date its section 1 prints as the end of the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `its footnotes` IS A LIST OF STRING

-- A later instrument read for item I1: what it carries on regulation 18, regulation 5 and chapter Gimel.
DECLARE `A later instrument read` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `its first printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its last printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `it carries an instruction on regulation 18, regulation 5 or chapter Gimel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how it was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`

-- A line of the consolidation (UNOFFICIAL), typed as the consolidation prints it. Always CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
DECLARE `A line of the consolidation` HAS
    `what the line is` IS A STRING
    `its words` IS A STRING
    `its amendment tags` IS A STRING
    `how it was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`

-- An item of the row, with its two limbs.
DECLARE `An item` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- ===== QUESTIONS ASKED OF THE VALUES =====

-- I1: does the string occur in the words of a regulation as printed?
GIVEN r IS A `A regulation as printed`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the regulation's words contain` MEANS CONTAINS (r's `its words`) w

GIVEN r IS A `A regulation as printed`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the regulation names the token` MEANS elem w (r's `the provisions it names, as tokens`)

GIVEN i IS AN `An item of an instrument`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the item's words contain` MEANS CONTAINS (i's `its words`) w

GIVEN i IS AN `An item of an instrument`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the item deletes words that contain` MEANS any (GIVEN d YIELD CONTAINS d w) (i's `the words it deletes`)

GIVEN a IS AN `An item of an instrument`, b IS AN `An item of an instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two items are two different items of one instrument` MEANS
    (a's `the instrument`'s `its issue number` EQUALS b's `the instrument`'s `its issue number`)
    AND (NOT (a's `its item number` EQUALS b's `its item number`))

-- I1: the print of a place is under the heading of the chapter an item repeals.
GIVEN p IS A `A regulation as printed`, i IS AN `An item of an instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is printed under the heading of the chapter the item repeals` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `the heading it is printed under`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST h THEN i's `the chapter it names` EQUALS JUST (h's `the chapter`)

-- I1: the provision lies outside the chapter the item repeals. This is the sentence of the red assertion.
GIVEN p IS A `A regulation as printed`, i IS AN `An item of an instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision lies outside the chapter the item repeals` MEANS
    NOT (`the provision is printed under the heading of the chapter the item repeals` p i)

GIVEN r IS A `A reference by number`, i IS AN `An item of an instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision the reference names lies outside the chapter the item repeals` MEANS
    `the provision lies outside the chapter the item repeals` (r's `the print of that place in 1995`) i

GIVEN r IS A `A reference by number`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the token is among the words of the citing regulation` MEANS
    CONTAINS (r's `the citing regulation`'s `its words`) (r's `the token the citing words print`)

GIVEN r IS A `A reference by number`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the place the token names is the place of the print typed beside it` MEANS
    r's `the place the token names` EQUALS r's `the print of that place in 1995`'s `its place`

-- I2: does the law print a numbered section with this number? It counts the numbers of the sections the law prints; a number inside a quoted paragraph is not one of them.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, l IS A `A law as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law prints a numbered section` MEANS any (GIVEN s YIELD s's `its number` EQUALS n) (l's `its sections`)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, o IS AN `An order as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the order prints a numbered section` MEANS any (GIVEN s YIELD s's `its number` EQUALS n) (o's `its sections`)

GIVEN l IS A `A law as printed`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of numbered sections the law prints` MEANS count (l's `its sections`)

-- I2: the numeral the quoted paragraph of a section of the law carries at its head.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, s IS A `A section as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section's quoted paragraph is headed by` MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the quoted paragraph it prints`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST q THEN q's `the number printed at its head` EQUALS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, l IS A `A law as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a section of the law prints a quoted paragraph headed by` MEANS
    any (GIVEN s YIELD `the section's quoted paragraph is headed by` n s) (l's `its sections`)

GIVEN w IS A STRING, s IS A `A section as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section's words contain` MEANS CONTAINS (s's `its words`) w

GIVEN w IS A STRING, s IS A `A section as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section's quoted paragraph contains` MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the quoted paragraph it prints`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST q THEN CONTAINS (q's `its words`) w

GIVEN w IS A STRING, fs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some footnote contains` MEANS any (GIVEN f YIELD CONTAINS f w) fs

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two instruments are two different issues` MEANS NOT (a's `its issue number` EQUALS b's `its issue number`)

-- I2: the title the opening words print before the defined term is the title of the law value the order binds the term to.
GIVEN o IS AN `An order as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the title in the opening words is the title of the law the term is bound to` MEANS
    o's `the title the opening words print before the defined term` EQUALS o's `the law the opening words define the term as`'s `its title`

GIVEN c IS AN `An item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`
